      ":question/problem": "![](images/f8/f87e0eb91b6ec47ca8a4d64c2824396e613123ed37862975b606608ff70445f0.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=5-2x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,5), B(2,1)$ and $C(3,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,5)$ results in a true statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (5)|= 5 - 2(0); 5|= 5✓$\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line:\n- Substituting the point $B(2,1)$ results in a true statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (1)|= 5 - 2(2); 1|= 1✓$\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line:\n- Substituting the point $C(3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (0)|= 5 - 2(3); 0|=-1\\cdot$\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line:"
    },
    ":knowledge-point/id": "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a",
